    "turn_text": "it hasn't dropped in the in the gas tank you know that a lot of a lot of inflation once it starts going up goes like cyclical so it'll go up some then a drop a little and go up again drop a little so you've got to look at it over the course of a quarter so it's hard to say that one month is going to be different i hope that it could trends down i think it's better for the american people that turns out i don't know if any policy that he could point to this that he's decreased inflation everything is is fighting inflation not drilling for oil not expanding natural gas they put a lot of money into the economy so i there's not any money in the economy that creates inflation So if he could point to his provisions in bidenomics that says this is an inflation fighter, they passed the inflation reduction act, but they put money into the economy. And so that was just the title that they put in. It doesn't have anything to do with dropping inflation. So you've got to look at it. If it goes down one month, that's absolutely great. I'm not going to say that's not. But if it goes up again, you've got to look at it as a trend and downwards, better than upward. But you got to look at it as a trend and I couldn't think of a policy that he's put forth. I do know because my family has a background in business and manufacturing. My family has a service that that people are coming back from work from COVID and our supply base is expanding and people are still buying cars and moving forward. So that's taking place. But we still have and sometimes you would say that's fighting what the government's actually",
